IMPORT prelude

-- Nurses and Midwives Act 1999 (Singapore) -- who may practise and call themselves a nurse or midwife (ss 26, 27, 2 and 19(10)),
-- employers and nurse's agents (ss 28, 29), Advanced Practice Nurse titles (s 35), practising-certificate renewal and surrender
-- (ss 18(4), (5), (7), (9), 19(6), (9)), discipline: grounds, sanctions, costs, appeal and re-registration (ss 19, 20, 21, 23),
-- temporary registration (s 16(3)), notice of changed particulars (s 13(3), (4)), refusal appeals (s 17(8)) and composition
-- of offences (s 43A).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NMA1999.txt. The deposit
-- describes itself as incorporating "all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later annotations are shown for
-- Act 11 of 2023 (wef 1 May 2023) and Act 19 of 2025 (wef 5 December 2025, which inserted s 43A and s 42(2A)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a nurse, midwife,
-- employer, agency or member of the public meets. Not encoded: the Board's constitution and meetings (ss 3 to 11), the
-- registration criteria of s 14 and the Board's discretions in ss 15 and 17 (beyond the refusal appeal), Advanced Practice
-- Nurse certification (s 32), inspectors' powers (s 36, except as context), Complaints Committees (ss 37 to 39), service of
-- documents (s 40), funds (s 42), the regulation-making power (s 44) and the transitional Part 7.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Nurses and Midwives Act 1999 -- practice`

DECLARE Person HAS
    `is a registered or enrolled nurse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered midwife` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registration or enrolment is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Advanced Practice Nurse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a supervised student nurse in an approved organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a supervised student midwife in an approved organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is rendering assistance in an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `26(2), 19(10) -- qualified nurse, qualified midwife`

-- s 26(2): "'qualified nurse' means a registered or enrolled nurse who holds a valid practising certificate authorising him or her
-- to practise nursing"; "'qualified midwife' means a registered midwife who holds a valid practising certificate".
-- s 19(10): where registration or enrolment "has been suspended ... the person is not to be regarded as being registered or
-- enrolled (as the case may be) for the purposes of this Act".
--
-- Registration alone is not enough: a registered nurse whose practising certificate has lapsed is not a "qualified nurse".
-- (The model uses one practising-certificate flag for both nursing and midwifery; the Act speaks of a certificate "authorising"
-- each. That simplification is the encoder's.)
GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualified nurse` IF
        `p`'s `is a registered or enrolled nurse`
    AND `p`'s `holds a valid practising certificate`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `registration or enrolment is suspended`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualified midwife` IF
        `p`'s `is a registered midwife`
    AND `p`'s `holds a valid practising certificate`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `registration or enrolment is suspended`)

§§ `26(1)(a), (b) -- using the title`

-- s 26(1)(a): any person who, "not being a qualified nurse, takes or uses the name or title of nurse in any language ... or any
-- name, title, addition, description, uniform or badge, implying that the person is a qualified nurse"; (b) the same for midwife.
-- Fine not exceeding $10,000 (no higher tier for a repeat offence, unlike ss 27 to 30).
GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the title nurse is an offence` IF
    NOT `is a qualified nurse` `p`

GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the title midwife is an offence` IF
    NOT `is a qualified midwife` `p`

§§ `35 -- Advanced Practice Nurse title`

-- s 35(a): any person who, "not being an Advanced Practice Nurse, takes or uses ... the name or title of Advanced Practice Nurse";
-- fine not exceeding $10,000. s 19(8): while certification is cancelled or suspended the person "is not to be regarded as being
-- certified as an Advanced Practice Nurse".
GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the title Advanced Practice Nurse is an offence` IF
    NOT `p`'s `is an Advanced Practice Nurse`

§§ `27 -- practising nursing or midwifery for reward`

-- s 27(1): "No person other than a qualified nurse may carry out any act of nursing for a fee or reward." (2): "No person other
-- than a qualified midwife may attend a woman at childbirth for a fee or reward."
-- (4), (5): students "undergoing a course" excepted if "under the supervision of a registered or enrolled nurse [registered
-- midwife]; and in an organisation approved by the Board". (6): (1) and (2) do not apply to "(a) a medical practitioner; (b) a
-- person rendering assistance in an emergency" or (c) a prescribed person (not modelled).
-- Unpaid nursing is outside s 27 altogether.
GIVEN `p` IS A Person, `for a fee or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying out nursing is an offence` IF
        `for a fee or reward`
    AND (NOT `is a qualified nurse` `p`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is a supervised student nurse in an approved organisation`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is a medical practitioner`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is rendering assistance in an emergency`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Person, `for a fee or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `attending a childbirth is an offence` IF
        `for a fee or reward`
    AND (NOT `is a qualified midwife` `p`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is a supervised student midwife in an approved organisation`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is a medical practitioner`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is rendering assistance in an emergency`)

-- s 27(3), 28(3), 29(2), 30: fine not exceeding $10,000 and, "in the case of a second or subsequent conviction, to a fine not
-- exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both".
GIVEN `a previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under sections 27 to 30` MEANS
    IF `a previous conviction` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `a previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under sections 27 to 30` MEANS
    IF `a previous conviction` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `28 -- employing an unqualified person`

-- s 28(1): "A person must not employ or engage a person who is not a qualified nurse to carry out any act of nursing." (No "fee or
-- reward" element.) (4): not applicable to employing "(a) a medical practitioner; (b) a person to care for (i) the person
-- employing or engaging him or her; or (ii) a family member, relative or friend" of the employer, or (c) a prescribed class.
-- (5): a defence "for a defendant to prove that (a) the defendant did not know ... and (b) the defendant had exercised due
-- diligence" -- both limbs.
GIVEN `the worker` IS A Person, `engaged to care for the employer or a family member, relative or friend` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the employer did not know` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer exercised due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employing the worker for nursing is an offence` IF
        (NOT `is a qualified nurse` `the worker`)
    AND (NOT `the worker`'s `is a medical practitioner`)
    AND (NOT `engaged to care for the employer or a family member, relative or friend`)
    AND (NOT (`the employer did not know` AND `the employer exercised due diligence`))

§§ `29 -- nurse's agents`

-- s 29(5): a "nurse's agent" is "a person who carries on, for a fee or reward, the business of arranging the supply of the services
-- of a nurse or a midwife". (1)(a): must not arrange for a person "who is not a qualified nurse to carry out any act of nursing";
-- (c) or arrange for a nurse or midwife "to work in contravention of the conditions of his or her registration or enrolment".
-- (3), (4): knowledge-plus-due-diligence defences. Unlike s 28, there is no carve-out for private carers.
GIVEN `the worker` IS A Person, `the agent did not know` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agent exercised due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agent's placement for nursing is an offence` IF
        (NOT `is a qualified nurse` `the worker`)
    AND (NOT (`the agent did not know` AND `the agent exercised due diligence`))

§§ `13(3), (4) -- changed particulars`

-- s 13(3): every registered nurse, enrolled nurse and registered midwife "must inform the Registrar in writing of any change in his
-- or her name, working address, residential address ... within 28 days of the change". (4): a report of a change of residential
-- address under s 10 of the National Registration Act 1965 is deemed compliance. A breach is a disciplinary ground (s 19(1)(b)),
-- not an offence.
GIVEN `days after the change` IS A NUMBER, `a residential address change reported under the National Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change was notified in time` IF
        `days after the change` AT MOST 28
    OR  `a residential address change reported under the National Registration Act`

§§ `16(3) -- temporary registration`

-- s 16(3): a temporary registration or enrolment "(a) must be for a period not exceeding 2 years; and (b) may be renewed for periods
-- not exceeding 12 months at a time".
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER, `is a renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the temporary registration period is permitted` IF
    IF `is a renewal` THEN `months` AT MOST 12 ELSE `months` AT MOST 24

§§ `17(7), (8) -- appeal against refusal to register`

-- s 17(8): a person aggrieved by a refusal to register or enrol "may, within one month of the notice ... appeal to the Minister whose
-- decision is final".
GIVEN `months after the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refusal appeal is in time` IF
    `months after the notice` AT MOST 1

§§ `18(4), (5) -- renewing the practising certificate`

-- s 18(4): renewal "must be made no later than one month before the expiry"; (5): one who applies "later than one month before the
-- expiry ... is liable to pay ... such late application fee as the Board may prescribe" (amount not in the Act).
GIVEN `months before expiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late application fee is payable` IF
    `months before expiry` LESS THAN 1

§§ `19 -- discipline`

-- s 19(1): the Board may act if satisfied the person "(a) has obtained his or her registration ... fraudulently or by a materially
-- incorrect statement; (b) has contravened section 13(3) or any condition ...; (c) has had his or her registration ... in a
-- territory outside Singapore, cancelled or suspended; (d) has been convicted of an offence ... which in the opinion of the Board
-- renders him or her unfit ...; (e) has been guilty of any misconduct, or negligence, which ... renders him or her unfit ...; (f) is
-- unable to perform satisfactorily the functions ... because of a mental or physical disability; (g) has not renewed his or her
-- practising certificate for a continuous period of not less than the prescribed period; or (h) is deceased."
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `obtained registration fraudulently`
    `contravened section 13(3) or a condition`
    `cancelled or suspended abroad`
    `convicted of an offence rendering unfit`
    `misconduct or negligence rendering unfit`
    `mental or physical disability`
    `practising certificate not renewed for the prescribed period`
    `deceased`

-- s 19(2)(b): suspension "for a period of not more than 2 years"; (d) "a financial penalty not exceeding $2,000".
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension period is permitted` IF
    `months` AT MOST 24

`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS 2000

-- s 18(7) and s 19(6): a person whose registration or enrolment is cancelled or suspended "on any of the grounds specified in
-- [section 19(1)](a) to (f)" must surrender the practising certificate and the certificate of registration or enrolment "within 14
-- days"; (18(9), 19(9)) failure is an offence, fine not exceeding $1,000. Grounds (g) and (h) carry no surrender duty.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground triggers the surrender duty` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `practising certificate not renewed for the prescribed period` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `deceased` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `days since cancellation or suspension` IS A NUMBER, `certificates surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to surrender is an offence` IF
        `the ground triggers the surrender duty` `the ground`
    AND `days since cancellation or suspension` GREATER THAN 14
    AND (NOT `certificates surrendered`)

`the maximum fine for failing to surrender` MEANS 1000

§§ `20 -- costs of the inquiry`

-- s 20(1): where there are grounds "under section 19(1)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f)", the Board may order the person to pay "such sums
-- as the Board thinks fit in respect of the costs and expenses of the inquiry". Not for (c) (cancelled abroad), (g) or (h).
GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `costs may be ordered` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `cancelled or suspended abroad` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `practising certificate not renewed for the prescribed period` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `deceased` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `21 -- appeal to the High Court`

-- s 21(1): a person aggrieved by a decision under s 19(2) or (3) "may, within 3 months of the date of the decision or within such
-- further period as the General Division of the High Court may allow, appeal". (2): "There is no appeal from a decision of the
-- General Division of the High Court."
GIVEN `months after the decision` IS A NUMBER, `the High Court allowed further time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disciplinary appeal is in time` IF
        `months after the decision` AT MOST 3
    OR  `the High Court allowed further time`

§§ `23 -- re-registration after cancellation`

-- s 23(3): where cancellation was "on any of the grounds referred to in section 19(1)(b) to (e), no application for the
-- re-registration ... may be made to the Board (a) before the expiry of 3 years from the date of the cancellation; or (b) more than
-- once in any period of 12 months".
-- Read literally, cancellation for fraud (ground (a)) or for disability (f) is not subject to the 3-year bar.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground carries the re-application bar` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `contravened section 13(3) or a condition` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancelled or suspended abroad` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `convicted of an offence rendering unfit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `misconduct or negligence rendering unfit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `years since cancellation` IS A NUMBER, `applied in the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a re-registration application may be made` IF
        (NOT `the ground carries the re-application bar` `the ground`)
    OR  (`years since cancellation` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `applied in the last 12 months`))

§§ `43A -- composition`

-- s 43A(1) (inserted by Act 19 of 2025): the Board may compound a prescribed compoundable offence by collecting "a sum not exceeding
-- the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $1,000."
-- (4): sums go to the Consolidated Fund.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 1000
